{"run_id": "20260830T125957-hepkg-269532", "qid": "gabriel-gf-01", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "780b816fd36c", "git_sha": "6840022-dirty", "question": "Which analyses are searches (rather than measurements) whose event selection uses both b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The following 18 analyses are searches that use both b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum in their event selection:\n\n- 2004.14060\n- 2006.05880\n- 2010.14293\n- 2012.03799\n- 2012.08600\n- 2102.01444\n- 2106.01676\n- 2106.14246\n- 2201.11585\n- 2202.08676\n- 2211.08028\n- 2302.05225\n- 2307.01094\n- 2403.01556\n- 2506.13565\n- 2508.13900\n- 2510.07527\n- 2511.11853\n\nNote that while these papers all use b-tagged jets and missing transverse momentum, they may use different algorithms or working points for b-tagging and different definitions of missing transverse momentum. For example, 2004.14060 uses track-based missing transverse momentum, while 2006.05880 uses \\(E_T^{\\text{miss}}\\).\", \"reason\": \"answered\", \"papers\": [\"2004.14060\", \"2006.05880\", \"2010.14293\", \"2012.03799\", \"2012.08600\", \"2102.01444\", \"2106.01676\", \"2106.14246\", \"2201.11585\", \"2202.08676\", \"2211.08028\", \"2302.05225\", \"2307.01094\", \"2403.01556\", \"2506.13565\", \"2508.13900\", \"2510.07527\", \"2511.11853\"]}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "facets", "args": {"field": "objects", "values": ["BJet", "MET"], "mode": "all", "category": "search"}, "rows": 18, "error": null, "seconds": 9.866}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": [], "seen_values": ["-tagged", "2004.1406", "2004.14060", "2006.0588", "2006.05880", "2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2012.086", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2201.11585", "2202.08676