{"run_id": "20260830T125957-hepkg-269532", "qid": "gen-conceptset-355bd42b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "780b816fd36c", "git_sha": "6840022-dirty", "question": "Which analyses measured Global Higgs boson signal strength modifier μ = σB(H→WW)/σB(H→WW)_SM?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses measured the Global Higgs boson signal strength modifier μ = σB(H→WW)/σB(H→WW)_SM:\n\n- 2004.04545: $CP$ Properties of Higgs Boson Interactions with Top Quarks in the $t\\bar{t}H$ and $tH$ Processes Using $H\\rightarrow\\gamma\\gamma$ with the ATLAS Detector\n- 2111.08340: Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using $H\\rightarrow b\\bar{b}$ decays in the ATLAS detector\n- 2504.13081: Combination and interpretation of differential Higgs boson production cross sections in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\n- 2510.07527: Combination of searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\n- 2602.18611: Effective coupling modifier fits (assuming no additional BSM decays and with B_inv, B_undet floating and |kappa_V|<=1 constraint)\n- 2604.21670: Effective field theory interpretation of ATLAS measurements involving the Higgs boson, electroweak bosons and the top quark\n- 2604.27044: Combined Run 3 resolved+merged HH->4b result and Combined Run 2 + Run 3 HH->4b result", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.04545", "2111.08340", "2504.13081", "2510.07527", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Global Higgs boson signal strength modifier μ = σB(H→WW)/σB(H→WW)_SM", "kind": "observable"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 35.592}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_measures_observable", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 110, "error": nul